      ],
      "updated": 1764100059154,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Decrypts the package\n& Installs on the client",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Decrypts the package\n& Installs on the client",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "EjXXGkzpQ-odpbXfzU5EI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -10711.566659371718,
      "y": 2308.0117221139544,
      "width": 1388.8834228515625,
      "height": 1155,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5D",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 482933013,
      "version": 2539,
      "versionNonce": 1582793443,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764100059154,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "E2E Publish Flow\n\n1. Package Upload\n   - The developer initiates a package upload from the UX or the Package Uploader Tool\n   - It sends the package and related files (EKB, Subval, etc) to the CMX Package API.\n2. Ingestion Process Begins\n   - The CMX Package API forwards the package to XPackage FD.\n   - XPackage FD sends it to the Ingest Workflow (WF).\n3. Ingest Workflow (WF) Processing\n   - ESRP Sign signs the package.\n   - MKMS decrypts the package using the developer’s EKB.\n   - Re-encrypts it using MKMS encryption.\n   - The package headers are updated with: VDUID and UVUID using ContentId.\n   - The encrypted package is sent to Blob Storage.\n4. Package Storage: The encrypted package is stored in the Blob Storage Account.\n   - CDN URIs are generated to access the package.\n5. Package Publishing Initiation: The developer initiates a Publish action\n6. CMX Modules Process the different Modules\n7. Publish Workflow (WF) Execution\n    - XPackage Publish WF is called to process packages from step #4.\n8. Publish WF communicates with XUS to register the package.\n9. Catalog receives the published package with all the other metadata details.\n10. xProduct processes the published product + metadata.\n11. The user initiates a 'Download' action from the Garrison App\n12. Packages CDN\n    - The Garrison system retrieves CDN URIs from XUS.\n    - These URIs point to the Packages CDN.\n    - The package is available for clients to download.\n13. Client decrypts the package & installs them locally\n    - The Garrison system decrypts the package.\n    - The decrypted package is installed on the client.\n14. Game install and package information goes through GPIDK/GRTS\n15. PC Gaming App Front Door (old front door) is used for sandbox/private audience/private catalog",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "E2E Publish Flow\n\n1. Package Upload\n   - The developer initiates a package upload from the UX or the Package Uploader Tool\n   - It sends the package and related files (EKB, Subval, etc) to the CMX Package API.\n2. Ingestion Process Begins\n   - The CMX Package API forwards the package to XPackage FD.\n   - XPackage FD sends it to the Ingest Workflow (WF).\n3. Ingest Workflow (WF) Processing\n   - ESRP Sign signs the package.\n   - MKMS decrypts the package using the developer’s EKB.\n   - Re-encrypts it using MKMS encryption.\n   - The package headers are updated with: VDUID and UVUID using ContentId.\n   - The encrypted package is sent to Blob Storage.\n4. Package Storage: The encrypted package is stored in the Blob Storage Account.\n   - CDN URIs are generated to access the package.\n5. Package Publishing Initiation: The developer initiates a Publish action\n6. CMX Modules Process the different Modules\n7. Publish Workflow (WF) Execution\n    - XPackage Publish WF is called to process packages from step #4.\n8. Publish WF communicates with XUS to register the package.\n9. Catalog receives the published package with all the other metadata details.\n10. xProduct processes the published product + metadata.\n11. The user initiates a 'Download' action from the Garrison App\n12. Packages CDN\n    - The Garrison system retrieves CDN URIs from XUS.\n    - These URIs point to the Packages CDN.\n    - The package is available for clients to download.\n13. Client decrypts the package & installs them locally\n    - The Garrison system decrypts the package.\n    - The decrypted package is installed on the client.\n14. Game install and package information goes through GPIDK/GRTS\n15. PC Gaming App Front Door (old front door) is used for sandbox/private audience/private catalog",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
