    },
    {
      "id": "MqpesTwdgl_Plx1zcCoTM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -13292.788898976214,
      "y": 12233.38974450959,
      "width": 1179.1593017578125,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAe",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 976127844,
      "version": 1301,
      "versionNonce": 2122816067,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764100059155,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Here’s a breakdown of the proposed POCs:\n\n    1. POC: Call into Xpackage WFs directly\n    Objective: Prove we can trigger the Xpackage Publish WFs without going through CMX frontends.\n    Goal: Ensure metadata is written to XUS as expected.\n    Validation: Use XUS Savant Handlers to inspect XUS state and confirm that the correct metadata is populated.\n    \n    2. POC: Write a minimal product configuration directly to XProduct\n    Objective: Define a lean config schema for PlayTest metadata (e.g., title, description, screenshot, etc).\n    Goal: Ensure Garrison can render a Product Detail Page (PDP) using the minimal config.\n    This gives us the ability to decouple from Catalog and simulate flight-specific PDPs.\n    \n    3. POC: Modify GRTS to simulate XUS behavior\n    Objective: Temporarily “fake” the XUS API responses that GRTS would eventually need from real XUS metadata.\n    Goal: Unblock downstream testing and simulate end-to-end functionality.\n    Once XUS is wired correctly (from Team Roshan’s work), we can remove the mocks and switch to the real integration.\n    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Here’s a breakdown of the proposed POCs:\n\n    1. POC: Call into Xpackage WFs directly\n    Objective: Prove we can trigger the Xpackage Publish WFs without going through CMX frontends.\n    Goal: Ensure metadata is written to XUS as expected.\n    Validation: Use XUS Savant Handlers to inspect XUS state and confirm that the correct metadata is populated.\n    \n    2. POC: Write a minimal product configuration directly to XProduct\n    Objective: Define a lean config schema for PlayTest metadata (e.g., title, description, screenshot, etc).\n    Goal: Ensure Garrison can render a Product Detail Page (PDP) using the minimal config.\n    This gives us the ability to decouple from Catalog and simulate flight-specific PDPs.\n    \n    3. POC: Modify GRTS to simulate XUS behavior\n    Objective: Temporarily “fake” the XUS API responses that GRTS would eventually need from real XUS metadata.\n    Goal: Unblock downstream testing and simulate end-to-end functionality.\n    Once XUS is wired correctly (from Team Roshan’s work), we can remove the mocks and switch to the real integration.\n    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4oQ2dy3hmCs_vFb2kQfFK",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12764.624947945937,
      "y": 9411.511722113955,
      "width": 204.4398651123047,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
