      "updated": 1764100059155,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Things to add:\n1. Creating the group\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Things to add:\n1. Creating the group\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "oEw48vXa9KFSoiWFmaMYY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -13266.267995383736,
      "y": 10577.469875649997,
      "width": 921.75927734375,
      "height": 1575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bAj",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 707852519,
      "version": 4851,
      "versionNonce": 1323443587,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1764100059155,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Dependencies:\n- XUS encrypting/decrypting packages\n- Changes needed to GRTS\n- Integrating into xProduct as a new Ingestion pipeline\n- Garrison for user experience (showing flight catalog, switching between flights)\n\nOpen Investigations / questions:\n- Group creation (do we build an abstraction layer or use vanilla DNA Groups)\n- How do we end the playtest i.e. how do we ensure XUS & xProduct know about it?\n    - How do we revoke the license?\n- Do we have all metadata for xpackage to publish to XUS?\n    - PublishJobParameters\n- What happens in xProduct when the developer 'Publishes' the product in Partner Center?\n    - Does xProduct merge the product metadata?\n    - Can we still continue to Playtest after game is launched? How does Garrison handle this?\n\n\nxFlight Config:\n- Flight name, description, image?\n- Start date / end date\n- Audience Group\n- Flight Visibility (private, public)\n\n\n- [One for Flighting all up] Terms of Use, Dev release notes\n\n\nxProduct:\n- How do you model Flighted products inside of xProduct?\n    - Create an alternate ingestion pipeline\n    - Add the needed fields we need for xFlight\n- How does Audience Group reflects visibility within Garrison?\n    - It can. Upto xFlight design.\n    - xProduct works with DNA Groups today.\n    - Has the flexibility on who can see, access, etc. It's based on 'verbs' that is flexible\n    - xProduct has a concept of Pri. Aud (isMemeberPartofGroup)\n- XTarget:\n    - XTarget: Engine that powers xPrice (can put a specific criteria based on needs)\n    - Allows to create campaigns \n- Can we have a channel of just flights in Garrison?\n    - Leverage ChannelService: It can call into xFlight\n    - Dynamic Channels: Based on queries (via xSearch) and hydrate the products\n- Xproduct has different Skus - release, pre-release, etc\n    - Diff sku per market (renewable period, licensing policy)\n    - ProductId001 - Release Sku; ProductId002 - pre-release sku\n    - Per flight metadata can live in xFlight config and link foreign key in xProduct\n- All Clients go through XP Services:\n    (e.g. Garrison: XPE; Mercury: XPC)\n    - We can abstract the info clients need to know however we want on the backend\n\nBig Scary Things:\n- In-app commerce integration (?)\n- Co-dev to get another ingestion partner added within xProduct (work w/ CJ)\n\nSME: Sagar Shah, Adam Smith\n(need to get this work prioritized as part of planning)\n\n\nXUS / SUCU:\n- Plan for Changing Licensing to support MSIXVC\n    - Timeline?\n    - What other scenarios does this power?\n- How do we revoke the license?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Dependencies:\n- XUS encrypting/decrypting packages\n- Changes needed to GRTS\n- Integrating into xProduct as a new Ingestion pipeline\n- Garrison for user experience (showing flight catalog, switching between flights)\n\nOpen Investigations / questions:\n- Group creation (do we build an abstraction layer or use vanilla DNA Groups)\n- How do we end the playtest i.e. how do we ensure XUS & xProduct know about it?\n    - How do we revoke the license?\n- Do we have all metadata for xpackage to publish to XUS?\n    - PublishJobParameters\n- What happens in xProduct when the developer 'Publishes' the product in Partner Center?\n    - Does xProduct merge the product metadata?\n    - Can we still continue to Playtest after game is launched? How does Garrison handle this?\n\n\nxFlight Config:\n- Flight name, description, image?\n- Start date / end date\n- Audience Group\n- Flight Visibility (private, public)\n\n\n- [One for Flighting all up] Terms of Use, Dev release notes\n\n\nxProduct:\n- How do you model Flighted products inside of xProduct?\n    - Create an alternate ingestion pipeline\n    - Add the needed fields we need for xFlight\n- How does Audience Group reflects visibility within Garrison?\n    - It can. Upto xFlight design.\n    - xProduct works with DNA Groups today.\n    - Has the flexibility on who can see, access, etc. It's based on 'verbs' that is flexible\n    - xProduct has a concept of Pri. Aud (isMemeberPartofGroup)\n- XTarget:\n    - XTarget: Engine that powers xPrice (can put a specific criteria based on needs)\n    - Allows to create campaigns \n- Can we have a channel of just flights in Garrison?\n    - Leverage ChannelService: It can call into xFlight\n    - Dynamic Channels: Based on queries (via xSearch) and hydrate the products\n- Xproduct has different Skus - release, pre-release, etc\n    - Diff sku per market (renewable period, licensing policy)\n    - ProductId001 - Release Sku; ProductId002 - pre-release sku\n    - Per flight metadata can live in xFlight config and link foreign key in xProduct\n- All Clients go through XP Services:\n    (e.g. Garrison: XPE; Mercury: XPC)\n    - We can abstract the info clients need to know however we want on the backend\n\nBig Scary Things:\n- In-app commerce integration (?)\n- Co-dev to get another ingestion partner added within xProduct (work w/ CJ)\n\nSME: Sagar Shah, Adam Smith\n(need to get this work prioritized as part of planning)\n\n\nXUS / SUCU:\n- Plan for Changing Licensing to support MSIXVC\n    - Timeline?\n    - What other scenarios does this power?\n- How do we revoke the license?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
